-# Three independent judges on three model families, then one synthesis.
-#
-# Lane choice: the three judge nodes ride the `*_lens` lanes (minimax_lens /
-# glm_lens / deepseek_lens) because those lanes exist exactly for
-# heterogeneous-family review — the user asked for MiniMax-M3, GLM-5.3, and
-# DeepSeek-Flash verdicts, and each family must judge alone so cross-family
-# disagreement is visible in the synthesis rather than averaged away by a
-# shared router. The synthesizer rides the `judge` lane (glm) on purpose:
-# synthesis is mechanical reconciliation, not a fourth vote, and keeping it
-# off the three judge families preserves "three families judged, one
-# composed" as a readable property of the panel.
-version: "1"
-task_class: session_task_judge
-
-nodes:
-  - { name: minimax_judge, type: researcher, model_lane: minimax_lens, prompt_ref: prompts/minimax-judge.md, dispatch_mode: parallel, gates: [budget_gate] }
