+version: "0.1.0"
+task_class: ui_feature_parity
+description: >
+  Spec gap-closure panel — 3 heterogeneous-family lenses (glm/minimax/opus)
+  read the mini-ork backend route surface, the current [redacted]-native-surface
+  spec, and the ui/ frontend, then each emits the DELTA: backend capabilities
+  not yet covered by an FR or not surfaced in the FE. Opus synthesizes the three
+  gap reports into a single backend→FE coverage matrix + the missing FRs, so the
+  implementation stage misses no feature.
+
+nodes:
+  - { name: planner,           type: planner,    model_lane: planner,      prompt_ref: prompts/planner.md,     dispatch_mode: serial }
+  # D-047: each lens routes to its NAMED family lane. glm (Zhipu) / minimax
+  # (MiniMax) / opus (Anthropic) are 3 distinct families → low-correlation
+  # detectors (Rajan 2025), so the union of their gap lists covers each
+  # single model's consistent blind spot. Opus doubles as the synthesizer
+  # (strongest reasoner for the merge), but decorrelation lives at the lens tier.
+  - { name: glm_lens,          type: researcher, model_lane: glm_lens,     prompt_ref: prompts/lens-glm.md,     dispatch_mode: parallel }
